{
   "name": "pg_pure",
   "abstract": "Write PostgreSQL functions in the Pure programming language",
   "description": "pg_pure embeds libpure to make Pure a procedural language in PostgreSQL, like PL/Perl or PL/Python. A function body is Pure code: term rewriting with pattern matching, exact rational and arbitrary-precision arithmetic, lazy streams, and symbolic computation, with database access through SPI. It provides a trusted language (pg_pure, pending a libpure sandbox) and an untrusted, superuser-only language (pg_pureu).",
